== bash-defined function stays lax after switching to kosh:
[]
ok
== kosh-defined function stays strict when called from bash mood:
is not set
== switching back to kosh restores strictness, and set -M prints the mood:
nounset-restored
sh
== sourced function keeps its source mood:
inside=bash unset=[]
outside=kosh
== strictness changes from a bash function reach a bash caller:
nounset=off
pipefail=off
failglob=off
== a bash function cannot relax the kosh mood:
nounset=on
pipefail=on
failglob=on
== propagated mood carries its strictness:
mood=sh unset=[]
rc-done
== source --mood runs a file in that mood and restores the mood:
inside=bash unset=[]
after=kosh status=0
inside=sh unset=[]
unknown-mood-status=1
